# Sleic Pin-Ball (SLEIC1) -- ONE four-player game, three balls each, twelve balls
# total.  Four credited START presses ~750 frames apart while ball 1 is still in
# play add players 1-4 (boxed "N JUGADOR(ES)" DMD announcement verified per-press:
# see task-3-report.md fix-round-1 section); the model then serves all twelve balls
# in the machine's own round-robin turn order (P1B1,P2B1,P3B1,P4B1,P1B2,...).
# Each player takes a different, constant number of lane hits per ball (1/2/3/4) so
# the four final scores differ.
